{"name":"Sinbad","hex":"#a6d5d0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sinbad","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A fictional sailor, the hero of a story-cycle of Middle Eastern origin, who encountered monsters and magic while travelling the seas east of Africa and south of Asia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sinbad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sinbad (comedian)","blocks":[{"text":"David Adkins, better known by his stage name Sinbad, is an American stand-up comedian and actor. He became known in the 1990s from being featured on his own HBO specials, appearing on several television series, most notably as Coach Walter Oakes in A Different World (1987–1991) and as David Bryan on The Sinbad Show (1993–1994). He has also appeared in films such as That's Adequate (1989), Coneheads (1993), Houseguest (1995), Jingle All the Way (1996), Good Burger (1997), Crazy as Hell (2002) and Planes (2013)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Entertainer_Sinbad.jpg/330px-Entertainer_Sinbad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinbad_(comedian)","wikidata":"Q558324"},{"title":"Sinbad (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Sinbad is a British action-adventure fantasy family saga television series that aired on Sky1 from 8 July to 23 September 2012. It was produced by Impossible Pictures, who previously made Walking with Dinosaurs and Primeval. The series stars Elliot Knight as the eponymous hero Sinbad."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a5/Sinbad_Tv_Series_Title.png/330px-Sinbad_Tv_Series_Title.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinbad_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q1441232"},{"title":"Sinbad the Sailor","blocks":[{"text":"Sinbad the Sailor is a fictional mariner and the hero of a story-cycle. He is described as hailing from Baghdad during the early Abbasid Caliphate. In the course of seven voyages throughout the seas east of Africa and south of Asia, he has fantastic adventures in magical realms by encountering monsters and witnessing supernatural phenomena. His travel cycle was added to the collection of the One Thousand and One Nights."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Having_balanced_my_cargo_exactly.jpg/330px-Having_balanced_my_cargo_exactly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinbad_the_Sailor","wikidata":"Q122018"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/Sinbad_with_students.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/Sinbad_with_students.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Sinbad meeting with Zama American High School students in September 2004","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASinbad_with_students.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/South_Indian_Tales_of_Sindbad_16th_Century.jpg/500px-South_Indian_Tales_of_Sindbad_16th_Century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/South_Indian_Tales_of_Sindbad_16th_Century.jpg/1280px-South_Indian_Tales_of_Sindbad_16th_Century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/South_Indian_Tales_of_Sindbad_16th_Century.jpg/500px-South_Indian_Tales_of_Sindbad_16th_Century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"South Indian Sindbad-namah, 16th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASouth_Indian_Tales_of_Sindbad_16th_Century.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com